s are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation" 13194139534680 true] [17592186303122 1113 #uuid "72a3fd90-5133-5a81-a0e8-33ac74b2d520" 13194139534680 true] [17592186303122 1145 "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303124 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303125 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303126 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303127 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303128 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534680 true] [17592186303123 1041 "selection" 13194